+- **The doc-vs-code gap is the dominant defect shape.** `docs/agent.md`
+  specifies **7 routing classes** and **7 context layers**; before this audit
+  the code had **2** routing classes (`classify_route` was a keyword two-way
+  test) and **1** context layer (a bare `question: str`). Grep the doc's nouns
+  against `apps/api/src` when auditing coverage — a file existing is not
+  evidence.
+- **Multi-turn was entirely absent.** No conversation-turn table anywhere;
+  `inbox_consumer.resolve_question` fetches only the single message body, and
+  `ChatwootClient` has only `send_message` / `fetch_message` — **no way to list
+  prior conversation messages**. That is the root cause, not a symptom.
+- Strongest areas (production-grade): tenant isolation/RLS, audit + citation
+  provenance, tool-gateway safety (5 risk levels, confirmation bound to
+  action_hash, postcondition verification), human handoff + lease race,
+  timeout/retry/circuit-breaker, observability (18 metrics + traces).
+- Weakest (Demo-grade): RAG tuning (every parameter hardcoded, no chunk
+  overlap, no query rewrite, no metadata filter), evaluation attribution
+  (cannot tell "retrieval wrong" from "generation wrong"), tool ecosystem
+  (only 4 tools registered, **no read/business tools at all**, no tool
+  selection logic), model routing (single model, no fallback chain).
