+### Benchmarks actually sourced (not invented)
+
+- containment: Teneo / Alhena / Talkative (via simpli.support) — Tier-1
+  agentic AI 60–90%, well-implemented 70–90%, e-commerce 70–80% typical /
+  89–92% leaders; Intercom Fin 76% at scale; MyAskAI's 195 deployments
+  (spread 15–98.3%, "the headline number hides everything").
+- **The pairing rule** (from both simpli.support and MyAskAI): contained
+  counts abandons and dead-ends, so it must always be read with CSAT and
+  reopen rate. That is why the plan targets reopen rate ≤5%.
+- latency: chatzybot — TTFT p50 <500ms, p95 <1.5s, p99 <3s, total backstop
+  15–20s, and **slice p95 by model / region / first-turn-vs-follow-up**.
+- cost: CallSphere — 0.2–0.5¢ simple, 3–15¢ complex multi-tool, ~$7 human,
+  cached tokens ~50% cheaper, and **p95 cost matters** (retry loops hide in the
+  mean). Hard limits: ≤10 LLM calls/conversation, log every limit-hit event.
+- RAG eval: RAGAS methodology explicitly **does not prescribe absolute
+  thresholds** — it says compare against your own baseline and treat it as a CI
+  regression gate. That is exactly what `release_check` +
+  `pytest_plugins_release` already do, so the plan says so rather than chasing
+  a vendor number. Also: 256/512/1024 chunk-size experiment set;
+  retrieve top-20 → rerank → top-5; faithfulness + context recall are the
+  highest-signal metrics.
